<description>&lt;p&gt;The UN top court has ruled that Myanmar committed genocide against the Rohingya minority, confirming the junta’s systematic attacks on the group. The junta has destroyed bridges in Arakan, moved west of the Sittaung River, and is planning a 108‑kilometre fence on the Bangladesh border while an airstrike hit a displacement camp in Rakhine. In Sagaing, junta forces killed 11 people as Starlink outages isolated communities and health-care facilities continued to be attacked in October 2026. Gold revenues now fund resistance groups and Myanmar-linked arsenic pollution is driving a clean-water scramble in Thailand. There were 2,332 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.euronews.com/2026/11/19/myanmar-guilty-of-genocide-against-rohingya-un-court-rules&quot;&gt;Euronews&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/15/myanmar-rohingya-genocide-icj&quot;&gt;The Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxNR1YxU1JOYjBqbWNwdEhQM3VmUTd0aF9jNE9LcU1XU3U3YTd5YXV5d2xncWgxR21lY1R3aHR4WGJoNG1wczZ1UV8ycnZfdnRLSVZQdGllRVZOZlhjTHJqUS1ub2FiajM1bmNhRGlXb2RIemVqUnRKSk85dzJXUUplWHZqM0VELVJqdFJpb3l5M3NHSFF3SWtZVXdzRWVCaWJtOUJ1TXpXN21Vam9RNjYybHFR?oc=5&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/11/19/world/myanmar-icj-ruling-genocide&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/18/world/asia/myanmar-rohingya-muslim-genocide-world-court.html&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/19/world/asia/myanmar-rohingya-village-refugee-genocide.html&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/11/19/icj-rules-myanmar-committed-genocide-against-the-ro